SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

Why AGPL: Folio's value is that users can verify documents stay local.
AGPL requires operators of hosted modified versions to share source, which
protects the project against closed hosted forks that cannot be audited.
Evaluated against MIT / Apache-2.0 / GPL-3.0: MIT and Apache-2.0 permit
closed hosted forks without source disclosure; GPL-3.0 covers distribution
but not network use. AGPL-3.0 closes the hosted-service gap.
